# Public keys allowed to log in to rama over SSH as james.
#
# chezmoi writes this file to ~/.ssh/authorized_keys, the only key file sshd
# reads (sshd-rama.conf). Deleting a line and applying revokes that key.
#
# PUBLIC KEYS ONLY. This repo is public. The private half is in 1Password and
# on each client, and is never committed anywhere.
#
# One key per line, with these options in front of it:
#
#   restrict   no port, agent or X11 forwarding, no pty, no ~/.ssh/rc.
#   pty        gives back the pty, so `ssh rama` works by hand.
#
# There is one key for rama, id_ed25519_rama, and every client holds a copy.
# It is used for rama alone. Each copy of the private key has a passphrase,
# which is what makes a copied key file useless. No from= address restriction:
# the firewall already limits logins to the LAN and the tailnet, and from=
# would lock a client out whenever its address changed.
#
# README.md, "Set up a client", has the steps for a new client, and "Replace
# the key" the steps for a new key.
#
# The options must be exactly `restrict` or `restrict,pty`. Script 09 fails the
# apply to name any other line, and warns while this file has no key line.

restrict,pty ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIOlx1N/RjnFh+GrLrLNGyYp2Sc4zjwFqYkDcjsc8J9CO id_ed25519_rama
